1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:02,120
It's okay, bhaiya…

2
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,373
this Diwali too…
you're not coming?

3
00:00:04,373 --> 00:00:08,807
Karan's in Bengaluru. Home with
Mummy-Papa… just Ishaan stayed.

4
00:00:08,807 --> 00:00:11,667
Papa's medicines,
the hospital runs…

5
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:14,389
alone. A thank-you? Never.

6
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:15,669
In the Ramayana too…

7
00:00:15,669 --> 00:00:17,866
one brother stayed home. Bharata.

8
00:00:17,866 --> 00:00:22,502
Rama left for the forest… Bharata?
He crowned Rama's sandals.

9
00:00:22,502 --> 00:00:27,070
And himself? In Nandigram, in bark
clothes… for fourteen years.

10
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,905
Ishaan is doing the same… in his
brother's place.

11
00:00:29,905 --> 00:00:33,172
For both of them… it wasn't a
burden. It was a trust.

12
00:00:33,172 --> 00:00:35,435
Reaching Nandigram, Bharata said…

13
00:00:35,435 --> 00:00:39,880
“Etad rajyam mama bhratra, dattam
sannyasavat svayam”…

14
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,532
My brother himself gave me this
kingdom, as a trust.

15
00:00:44,662 --> 00:00:48,172
That night Karan… booked the
Friday train. And said…

16
00:00:48,172 --> 00:00:49,276
“Thank you, Ishaan.”

17
00:00:49,276 --> 00:00:52,265
Which one are you… the one who
stayed? Or the one who left?
